  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Pinned NLopt 2.11.0-dev revision 6e6593f with Luksan disabled and a fail-closed five-source permissive closure; implemented a bounded one-import callback Wasm reactor and JavaScript host for exact explicit nlopt-nelder-mead and nlopt-cobyla identities; independently qualified 5 Nelder-Mead and 7 feasible COBYLA envelopes plus deliberate infeasibility rejection against SciPy 1.18/PRIMA; proved packed objective/gradient/constraint/Jacobian layouts, bounds, finite/memory/ABI guards, force-stop budgets, failure cleanup, lifecycle/reuse, real Chromium behavior, and the exact artifact on Linux x64/ARM64, macOS ARM64, and Windows x64. Automatic selection remains disabled.",
    "risks": [
      "NLopt can return a positive termination code for an infeasible COBYLA point, so central NumericalResult integration must independently recompute objective, bounds, residuals, feasibility, and applicable local-optimum evidence.",
      "The current integration base has pre-existing unclassified cminpack and MGH C adapters and an approximation capability-record test mismatch; these block the shared architecture and numerics gates before this isolated backend can be integrated.",
      "bench-1 rejects the available SSH identity, so the Linux x64 portability receipt is from the local x64 host rather than that persistent host.",
      "The browser cooperative receipt proves a pre-set shared-atomic force-stop; hard interruption of a non-returning callback is correctly provided by terminating and replacing its worker."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Cherry-pick this lane commit into the integration branch and classify src/adapter.c as a foreign-library host adapter in architecture/native-code.json together with the inherited cminpack/MGH classifications.",
      "Register the reactor, exact import/export surface, package ownership, and lazy resource beside cminpack in shared integration manifests; do not enable automatic selection.",
      "Expose the two exact methods through the ordinary-Python optimization router, preserve correct dynamic fallbacks, and fail explicit NLopt requests rather than silently changing method identity.",
      "Independently validate every public result, then rerun the source-bound corpus, release verifier, Chromium test, four-platform portable smoke, shared numerics suite, and architecture gate on the integrated candidate."
    ]
  }
